@startuml phonetic-route-decision
' Rules route (RewriteWfst, no feature) vs regex route (PhoneticWfst/PhoneticNfaWfst, phonetic-rules).
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  DiamondBackgroundColor #EAECEE
  DiamondBorderColor #707B7C
  DiamondFontColor #2C3E50
  ArrowColor #34495E
  BorderColor #34495E
  BackgroundColor #EAECEE
}
title Phonetic matching — rules route vs. regex route

start
:Phonetic / sound-alike matching;
if (How is the sound-alike mapping specified?) then (fixed rewrite rules)
  :**RewriteWfst**
  + **CommonPhoneticRules** :: english / german / french
  no feature gate — always available; <<#D6EAF8>>
  note right #D1F2EB
    Use when: a small set of deterministic
    substitutions (ph->f, ck->k) suffices.
    Zero build config; composes with any
    LevenshteinWfst via compose(rewrite, lev).
  end note
  stop
else (a phonetic regex pattern)
  :**PhoneticWfst**<D> / **PhoneticNfaWfst**
  Thompson NFA over "(ph|f)one"
  feature = "phonetic-rules"; <<#D6EAF8>>
  note right #D1F2EB
    Use when: alternation / character classes /
    wildcards are needed, or you want the pattern
    compiled once into an NFA-backed transducer.
  end note
  stop
endif
@enduml
